# SCALE readout — the shorter cut of (thresh)Hold The Line.
#
# Same argument, roughly two thirds of the slides: for a readout rather than a
# talk, where the room wants the shape of the work and will ask about the parts
# it cares about. What comes out, and why each one is the safe thing to lose:
#
#   Preference (the whole section)  — the second axis. It is the one part that
#       stands alone: everything before it is the threshold where the *data*
#       says, and Regions after it never refers back. Dropping it costs a
#       section, not an argument.
#   gmm-em      "Great Expectations" — an aside explaining EM to a room that
#       may not need it. The slide before it says "fit a two-component Gaussian
#       mixture" and the slide after it does not depend on how.
#   anchored-em "Vote of Confidence" — the mechanism drawing under the anchored
#       fit. The claim survives on anchored-gmm alone; this is the how.
#   blend-schedule "Never Hand Over Completely" — the weighting on the average.
#       A refinement of the slide before it, and a good answer to a question.
#   the appendix — both slides after The End, which exist to be brought up if
#       someone asks and cannot be in a deck that is being cut for length.
#
# Four fragments carry a `.scale` variant, and every one of them is the *notes*
# rather than the slide: a note that pointed at a slide this cut removes. See
# `slides/README.md` on variants. Nothing else differs, so a change to the
# figure or the headline of xcal, blend, anchored-gmm or split-fraction has to
# be made in both files — which is the price of the suffix mechanism and the
# reason only four fragments pay it.
#
# The outline is its own fragment because this deck has four sections and not
# five (`slides/STYLE.md`), so it appears five times: bare, then +at1 … +at4.

theme: vtsearch

slides:
  title-hold-the-line
  outline-scale-readout

  # 1 — VTSearch
  outline-scale-readout +at1
  problem
  make-detector
  train-loop
  find-results
  find-line
  embed-flow
  vote-boundary

  # 2 — Calibration
  outline-scale-readout +at2
  xcal.scale
  gmm-idea
  blend.scale
  anchored-gmm.scale
  quantile-transfer
  split-fraction.scale

  # 3 — Regions
  outline-scale-readout +at3
  voting-modes
  evt-midpoint
  evt-gumbel
  evt-close

  # 4 — The End
  outline-scale-readout +at4
